      "text": "Let's start by examining the expression $(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)$.\n\nWe will use the tangent addition formula for angles that sum to 45 degrees. The formula is:\n\\[\n\\tan(A + B) = \\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}\n\\]\nSetting \\(A = 20^\\circ\\) and \\(B = 25^\\circ\\), we get:\n\\[\n\\tan(20^\\circ + 25^\\circ) = \\tan 45^\\circ\n\\]\nSince \\(\\tan 45^\\circ = 1\\), we have:\n\\[\n1 = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ}\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nRearranging the terms, we get:\n\\[\n1 = \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nAdding 1 to both sides, we obtain:\n\\[\n2 = 1 + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nThis can be factored as:\n\\[\n2 = (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\n\\]\nThus, the value of $(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)$ is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
