      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the expression \\((1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\\), we can use trigonometric identities and properties. Let's proceed step by step.\n\nFirst, recall the tangent addition formula:\n\\[\n\\tan(A + B) = \\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B}\n\\]\nWe can use this formula to find \\(\\tan 45^\\circ\\), since \\(45^\\circ = 20^\\circ + 25^\\circ\\). Therefore,\n\\[\n\\tan 45^\\circ = \\frac{\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ}{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ} = 1\n\\]\nThis implies:\n\\[\n\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ = 1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nNow, let's multiply the original expression by 1 in a clever way:\n\\[\n(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) = 1 + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\n\\]\nUsing the identity \\(\\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ = 1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ\\), we substitute:\n\\[\n1 + \\tan 20^\\circ + \\tan 25^\\circ + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = 1 + (1 - \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ) + \\tan 20^\\circ \\tan 25^\\circ = 1 + 1 = 2\n\\]\nTherefore, the value of the expression \\((1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ)\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
