      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "We know that $\\tan(45^\\circ - \\theta) = \\frac{1 - \\tan \\theta}{1 + \\tan \\theta}.$ So, let $\\theta = 20^\\circ,$ and we have $\\tan 25^\\circ = \\frac{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ}{1 + \\tan 20^\\circ}.$ Plugging this into the expression, we get:\n\\begin{align*}\n(1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)(1 + \\tan 25^\\circ) &= (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)\\left(1 + \\frac{1 - \\tan 20^\\circ}{1 + \\tan 20^\\circ}\\right) \\\\\n&= (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)\\left(\\frac{1 + \\tan 20^\\circ + 1 - \\tan 20^\\circ}{1 + \\tan 20^\\circ}\\right) \\\\\n&= (1 + \\tan 20^\\circ)\\left(\\frac{2}{1 + \\tan 20^\\circ}\\right) \\\\\n&= \\boxed{2}.\n\\end{align*}\nThe answer is: 2",
